# Implementation plan — Spec 1.4.0

## Summary

Spec 1.4.0 delivers **four embeddable Media iframe surfaces** — upload dialog (with optional image crop), lightweight file selector, inline media viewer (view/edit), and full scoped library dialog — so consumer microservices embed Media-owned UI instead of duplicating upload, browse, crop, or preview logic. Work spans **`media/`** (new routes and components), **`packages/media-embed/`** (URL builders, message types, hooks), and a **WebOnOne v2** reference consumer adoption. All surfaces follow the 1.1.0 embed contract: `parentOrigin` query, JWT via `webonone:media:init`, results via typed postMessage. See [01-overview.md](./01-overview.md) and [02-media-iframe-components.md](./02-media-iframe-components.md).

## Branch and prerequisites

| Item | Value |
|------|--------|
| Branch | `spec/1.4.0` (checkout + pull before each phase) |
| Base | `master` |
| Package builds | `npm run build:media-embed` before consumer prod build; WebOnOne chains via `webonone-v2/package.json` |
| Migrations | None — reuses 1.1.0 schema |
| Env | `VITE_MEDIA_ORIGIN` + `VITE_MEDIA_API_BASE_URL` in consumer; route URLs derived in `mediaConfig.ts` — no per-route `VITE_*` |
| JWT | `JWT_SECRET` duplicated in `media/backend/.env` (matches Identity) |

Existing routes `/picker` and `/upload` remain unchanged. Reference patterns: `PickerPage.tsx`, `UploadPage.tsx`, `EmbedLayout.tsx`, `packages/media-embed/src/embedUrl.ts`.

